{"toolCallId":"call_146933f1f2c44abba1efc9df0676f6e7","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given an invocation that writes a warning to stderr, When the same arguments run with `--quiet`, Then stderr carries the same warning bytes as the default run and stdout holds the level line alone | `diff <(bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 >/dev/null) <(bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 >/dev/null)` prints nothing | Unmet | - |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:96:| REQ-007 | Under `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:77:- [ ] T016 Keep warnings on stderr under quiet, REQ-007 (`runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`). Verify: `diff <(bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 >/dev/null) <(bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 >/dev/null)` prints nothing.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"0430af","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
